%[text] %[text:anchor:H_D81E8B5D] #### Measure motor shaft velocity
%[text] DC motor position and velocity can be calculated from the output of an encoder. As the motor shaft spins, the encoder generates a signal that switches between high and low logic values. Each time the signal switches, the encoder counter is iterated. The number of times that the encoder switches for each turn of the motor shaft is a known value. For the virtual model, the default is 64 counts per revolution (CPR) of the motor shaft.
